  "title": "Motor Imagery dataset from Weibo et al 2014",
  "description": "A 60-channel EEG dataset from 10 healthy, BCI-naive participants performing simple limb motor imagery (left hand, right hand, feet) and compound limb motor imagery (both hands, left hand with right foot, right hand with left foot), plus a rest condition. The recordings were used to examine EEG oscillatory patterns (ERD/ERS), cognitive processes, and effective connectivity during motor imagery. This is a preprocessed (bandpass filtered, downsampled to 200 Hz) BIDS version curated through MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a Neuroscan SynAmps2 amplifier (60 EEG channels plus 2 EOG, nose reference, 0.5-100 Hz online bandpass, 50 Hz notch). Participants performed kinesthetic motor imagery in response to visual text cues (1 s cue, 4 s imagery, 8 s trials), with 560 trials across 8 sections. Data were bandpass filtered at 0.5-50 Hz and downsampled to 200 Hz.",
